          "For Christians, Abraham’s legacy reaches its fullest meaning within the story of Jesus Christ. Galatians 3 connects God’s promise to Abraham with the blessing reaching the nations through Christ. Romans 4 presents Abraham as an example of faith and explains that God’s promise is received by faith. The Christian understanding is therefore not that Abraham earned salvation through a perfect life, but that his story points toward trust in God and the fulfilment of God’s saving purpose through Jesus.",
          "Abraham was not flawless. He experienced fear, made mistakes, and sometimes tried to secure the future through human arrangements. Yet his life repeatedly returned to the question of whether he would trust God. His legacy is not perfection; it is a life shaped by a promise that reached beyond his own lifetime."
